# Single Transferable Vote Implementation

This repository has a simple implementation of the Single Transferable Vote system

## How it works
The algorithm works on ballots, vectors which at position i hold all the candidates of rank i.

A single voter has a weight, that starts as 1 and "decays" depending on what fraction of the voter's vote has been used for elected candidates. E.g.: if candidate A gets elected with 150% of the threshold votes, each voter who elected them contributes 2/3 of their vote towards that candidate, and their weight gets multiplied by 1/3.

The weight also keeps track of ties: since multiple candidates can be tied in a ballot, each one of them gets an equal share of the vote if they are still in the race. E.g. if candidate A,B,C,D are tied, but B is out of the rac, each candidate gets 1/3 of the vote and the weight gets temporarily divided by three.

At each step the algorithm works as follows:
- Look for a candidate still in the race who has at least 1/(candidates to elect) of the votes and elect them.
- If no one was found, find all of the candidates with the least number of votes and disqualify them.
- In both cases, transfer the vote as follows:
    - for elected candidates, calculate the fraction of surplus votes. Multiply the vote share of each elector by that fraction and then either redistribute it among the candidates tied with the just elected one or pass it to the next ranked candidates and subdivide it among them.
    - for disqualified candidates, follow the same procedure but without decaying the vote. 

## Results
The election can have three different outcomes:
1. The election was run normally, in which case all the elected candidates have reaches the threshold
2. Due to some voters not fully ranking all candidates, some vote shares become unused and thus not enough candidates are mathematically able to reach the threshold. In this case the election continues normally until the still running unelected candidates are in equal number as the unassigned seats. They get then marked as elected but with missing votes.
3. At a certain point, disqualifying multiple tied candidates would have led to less candidated being in the race than the number of unassigned seats. The election gets interrupted, the candidates with higher votes than these last place tied ones get marked as elected with missing votes like in scenario 2. and all the tied candidated get returned too.


## Functions and Classes
The `ballot_generator.rs` file implements `create_n_ballots`, that generates N ballots randomly according to the given parameters.
The `voting_systems.rs` file implements the `SingleTrasferableVote` class that holds data and runs the election. The results are then found in the public attribute `SingleTrasferableVote.results`, which has an instance of the `ElectionResult` class, structured as follows.
- `result`: an enum which encodes which of the three previously explained scenarios was encountered, respectively with the values `EveryWinnerAtCutoff`,`SomeElectedUnderCutoff`,`StoppedBecauseOfTie`, or that the election was not run: `NotRunElection`.
- `elected_candidates`: in every scenario holds all the candidates elected because they reached the threshold.
- `remaining_elected_candidates`: in scenarios 2. and 3. holds the candidated that were still in the race at the end/interruption of the election but didn't reach the threshold.
- `tied_at_interruption`: only in the third scenario, holds all the tied candidates with the least amount of votes that caused the election to stop.
